::GEO_U02_L03_Q04::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L03_Q04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.3<br><br>Question:<br>Point A(2, 1) moves to A(5, 1), then to A(5, -1). Which sequence matches? {
~ Reflect across x-axis, then translate right 3#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
~ Translate left 3, then reflect across y-axis#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
~ Rotate 90 degrees, then translate#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
= Translate right 3, then reflect across x-axis#Correct. This answer matches the lesson concept and uses transformation evidence.
}

