Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L03_Q05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.4<br><br>Question:<br>A repeated border slides 6 units right and matches exactly. What symmetry is shown? {
= Translation symmetry#Correct. This answer matches the lesson concept and uses transformation evidence.
~ Rotation symmetry#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
~ Reflection symmetry#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
~ No symmetry#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
}

::GEO_U02_L03_Q06::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L03_Q06<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.3<br><br>Question:<br>Why does transformation order matter? {
~ Order never changes an image#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
= Each step acts on the image from the previous step#Correct. This answer matches the lesson concept and uses transformation evidence.
~ Only reflections use order#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
~ Order matters only for color#This choice reflects a misconception about transformation sequences or symmetry. Check the order of transformations and the evidence that maps the figure.
}

